/// graphics — Native Graphics Library for Sounio
///
/// Pixel-based drawing and scientific plotting without external dependencies.
///
/// ## Modules
///
/// - `drawing` — Core primitives: Point2D, Color, Rect
/// - `surface` — RGBA pixel surface with line and rect drawing
/// - `export` — PPM output (pure Sounio), PNG stub (pending FFI)
/// - `plot` — Raster line plots with auto-scaling
/// - `scatter` — Raster scatter plots with cross markers
/// - `heatmap` — Raster heatmaps with color interpolation
/// - `quality` — Publication-oriented scientific raster plots: antialiased line/heatmap/contour, uncertainty bands, markers, error bars, histogram, ECDF, boxplot, violin density
/// - `epistemic` — Confidence bands, decay curves, and advanced epistemic visualization primitives (pure Sounio)
/// - `svg` — Vector export bridge (SVG markup to stdout)
/// - `tile` — TiledSurface for resolutions beyond 256×256
/// - `view` — Terminal image viewer (`show`, `render_surface`, `show_tiled`) using Unicode half-blocks + truecolor. Perfect for rapid iteration on epistemic figures.
///
/// ## Known Limitation
///
/// Due to a compiler bug with mutable references to structs containing large
/// arrays, write operations on `Surface` take and return the surface by value
/// rather than using `&!Surface`. This is a pragmatic workaround documented in
/// the implementation; it will be reverted once the codegen fix lands.
///
/// ## Design
///
/// This is the Phase 1 scaffold per `docs/design/native_graphics_library.md`.
/// The current implementation is stitched across the design/scaffold/quality lanes:
/// Grok owns the architecture brief, the scaffold lane materialized the base
/// graphics modules, and the quality lane adds SOTA scientific plot primitives.
/// All 5 moves for "best everything" epistemic visualization completed in parallel:
/// 1. Full glyph variety (shapes + uncertainty rings)
/// 2. ProvenanceLegend (SVG + helpers)
/// 3. Placement helpers
/// 4. TiledSurface integration (via view + primitives)
/// 5. EpistemicCurveFigure builder skeleton
/// Plus real terminal image viewer (graphics::view) so you can actually see the graphs inside Sounio.
///
/// ## Quick Start
///
/// ```sio
/// use graphics::surface::{Surface, surface_new, surface_clear, surface_draw_line}
/// use graphics::drawing::{color_black, color_white, color_red}
/// use graphics::export::export_ppm
///
/// fn main() with IO, Mut, Panic, Div {
///     var s = surface_new(100, 100)
///     s = surface_clear(s, color_white())
///     s = surface_draw_line(s, 10, 10, 90, 90, color_red())
///     export_ppm(&s)
/// }
/// ```
